      "id": 1,
      "text": "Ironia was born in 1871 when Randolph Township carved out a new community to serve the booming iron industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.njskylands.com/tnironia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name reflects its roots: Ironia was intended as the missing link along the rich ore vein that ran from the Dickerson Mine south into Chester.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.njskylands.com/tnironia",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 1869 railroad line opened through Ironia, passing the Black River and bringing passenger and freight service to the isolated woodland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.njskylands.com/tnironia",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
